  <section class="row" aria-labelledby="why-repair-title">
    <h2 id="why-repair-title">Why repair a chip now</h2>
    <div class="row-body">
      <p>A rock chip from the highway looks small, but Texas heat, cold fronts, and road vibration can turn it into a long crack overnight. Once a crack spreads, repair is usually off the table and you're looking at a full windshield replacement.</p>
      <p>A windshield chip repair fills the damage with a clear resin that bonds the glass back together and stops the break from growing. It restores strength, and in most cases makes the chip much harder to see.</p>
      <ul class="why-list">
        <li><strong>Faster.</strong> Most repairs take well under an hour.</li>
        <li><strong>More affordable.</strong> A fraction of the cost of a new windshield.</li>
        <li><strong>Keeps your factory glass.</strong> Your original windshield and its seal stay in place.</li>
        <li><strong>No ADAS calibration needed.</strong> Your camera stays where it is, so there's nothing to recalibrate.</li>
      </ul>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/#quote">Get a free repair quote</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row" aria-labelledby="can-repair-title">
    <h2 id="can-repair-title">Can my windshield be repaired?</h2>
    <div class="row-body">
      <p>It depends on the size, depth, and location of the damage. As a general rule, these are often good repair candidates:</p>
      <ul class="why-list">
        <li><strong>Rock chips</strong> smaller than a quarter, including bullseye, star, and combination breaks.</li>
        <li><strong>Short cracks</strong> that haven't spread far from the impact point.</li>
        <li><strong>Damage outside your direct line of sight</strong> on the driver's side.</li>
        <li><strong>Damage away from the edge</strong> of the glass.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Long cracks, damage at the edge of the windshield, or a chip right in front of the driver usually call for replacement. Send us a photo and we'll tell you honestly whether a repair will hold or whether <a href="/services/#windshield">windshield replacement</a> is the smarter call, even when repair is the cheaper job for you.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="row" aria-labelledby="how-repair-title">
    <h2 id="how-repair-title">How mobile windshield repair works</h2>
    <div class="row-body">
      <ul class="why-list">
        <li><strong>Send a photo or call.</strong> Tell us where you are and what the damage looks like.</li>
        <li><strong>We come to you.</strong> Home, work, or a parking lot anywhere in our <a href="/service-area/">service area</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>We clean and fill the chip.</strong> Resin is injected under pressure and cured to bond the glass.</li>
        <li><strong>You're done.</strong> Drive away the same day, with the repair backed by our workmanship warranty.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Until we get there, keep the chip clean and dry. A piece of clear tape over it helps, and avoid blasting the defroster or AC straight at the glass.</p>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/#quote">Ask about a repair</a>
    </div>
  </section>
